 "steps": [
  {
   "id": "first-shots",
   "title": "Buford holds the western ridges",
   "time": "Wed 1 July, c. 7:30",
   "narrative": "Lee's army was scattered across Pennsylvania, and neither commander meant to fight at Gettysburg. On the morning of 1 July two brigades of Heth's division came east along the Chambersburg Pike. Just west of the town they met the vedettes of John Buford's cavalry. Buford had chosen to delay on Herr, McPherson and Seminary Ridges. His dismounted troopers fired breech-loading carbines from fences and trees. They bought the hours the Union infantry needed to reach the stronger hills south of town.",
