  {
   "id": "north-collapse",
   "title": "Ewell hits from the north",
   "time": "Wed 1 July, 2:00 - 4:00 pm",
   "narrative": "Heth, now with Pettigrew and Brockenbrough, renewed the attack at 2:30. The 26th North Carolina, the army's largest regiment at 839 men, left the day with about 212. Pender's division then drove the I Corps through the seminary grounds. Meanwhile two of Ewell's divisions, Rodes and Early, arrived from the north. Barlow had advanced the XI Corps to a knoll that stuck out of the line. Early overran him and the Union right folded up.",
   "positions": {
