   "narrative": "Lee now planned an attack on the Union II Corps on Cemetery Ridge. Pickett's division and six brigades from Hill's corps would make it under Longstreet. Longstreet argued that it would fail, but obeyed. Around 1:00 pm between 150 and 170 Confederate guns opened what was probably the largest bombardment of the war. Hunt saved the Union ammunition, then about 15 minutes later about 80 Union guns replied. The Confederates were short of shells, and the Union line was little hurt.",
