   "narrative": "When the guns went quiet, between 10,500 and 12,500 Confederates stepped out of the trees and crossed three-quarters of a mile of open ground toward Cemetery Ridge. Union guns on Cemetery Hill and Little Round Top raked their flank, and musket and canister fire came from Hancock's line. At a bend in a low stone wall known as the Angle the Union line broke, and Armistead's brigade got in to the guns. Reinforcements sealed the breach. Nearly half of the attackers did not come back, and Pickett's division lost about two thirds of its men.",
