   "title": "Cavalry fights and the end of the battle",
   "time": "Fri 3 July, afternoon - evening",
   "narrative": "Two cavalry fights ran alongside the infantry assault. About three miles northeast of the town Stuart tried to get behind the Union line, but Gregg and Custer stopped him in a sabre melee. South of Big Round Top, after Pickett failed, Kilpatrick sent Farnsworth's brigade against entrenched infantry over rough ground. Farnsworth was killed in the fourth of five failed charges. Lee withdrew to Seminary Ridge, and on 4 July he began his retreat toward the Potomac.",
